1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,162
WWW.MY-SUBS.CO

﻿1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
- Synced and corrected by <font color="#009BCB"><b>chamallow</b></font> -
- www.MY-SUBS.com -

2
00:00:06,083 --> 00:00:08,957
My brother gave his life hunting Sauron.

3
00:00:08,958 --> 00:00:10,375
His task is now mine.

4
00:00:11,708 --> 00:00:14,915
This mark's very existence
proves Sauron escaped.

5
00:00:14,916 --> 00:00:16,749
The question now is, where?

6
00:00:16,750 --> 00:00:17,832
The evil is gone.

7
00:00:17,833 --> 00:00:19,375
Then why is it not gone from in here?

8
00:00:19,500 --> 00:00:23,332
These heroes shall be granted
a passage across the sea

9
00:00:23,333 --> 00:00:26,541
to the Undying Lands of Valinor.

10
00:00:30,083 --> 00:00:31,332
You're a deserter, aren't you?

11
00:00:31,333 --> 00:00:33,624
Duty demanded I return to Middle-earth.

12
00:00:33,625 --> 00:00:35,415
Was that the mark of your people's king?

13
00:00:35,416 --> 00:00:36,541
My people have no king.

14
00:00:36,666 --> 00:00:37,915
You are more than you claim.

15
00:00:37,916 --> 00:00:41,040
Your people have no
king, for you are him.

16
00:00:41,041 --> 00:00:42,707
Come with me to Middle-earth.

17
00:00:42,708 --> 00:00:45,124
And together we will
redeem both our bloodlines.

18
00:00:45,125 --> 00:00:48,165
Be careful. I am not the hero you seek.

19
00:00:49,750 --> 00:00:51,457
You remember me?

20
00:00:51,458 --> 00:00:52,624
No.

21
00:00:54,125 --> 00:00:58,249
After Morgoth's defeat, I killed Sauron.

22
00:00:58,250 --> 00:00:59,250
I do not believe you.

23
00:01:00,791 --> 00:01:02,415
I feel like he's my responsibility.

24
00:01:02,416 --> 00:01:04,332
- You feel like everyone is.
- No.

25
00:01:04,333 --> 00:01:06,750
He could've landed
anywhere, and he landed here.

26
00:01:06,875 --> 00:01:10,750
This stranger isn't a Man, or an Elf...

27
00:01:11,316 --> 00:01:12,333
He's something else.

28
00:01:12,334 --> 00:01:14,332
Á kuita!

29
00:01:14,333 --> 00:01:16,583
Get back!

30
00:01:17,916 --> 00:01:19,166
This is how we help him.

31
00:01:20,625 --> 00:01:23,250
He wants us to help
him find those stars.

32
00:01:25,250 --> 00:01:27,665
- Where are you goin'?
- To help my friend.

33
00:01:27,666 --> 00:01:31,457
You're my best friend in
this whole wide, wild world.

34
00:01:31,458 --> 00:01:33,040
Do you remember anything more yet?

35
00:01:33,041 --> 00:01:37,791
More has come. But to discover the
rest, I know I must go to Rhûn.

36
00:01:38,666 --> 00:01:40,666
Sounds a bit like an adventure.

37
00:01:42,625 --> 00:01:45,874
The light of the Eldar is fading.

38
00:01:45,875 --> 00:01:49,957
Despite our every effort, our
decline has only quickened.

39
00:01:49,958 --> 00:01:53,957
If the Elves abandon
Middle-earth, it will be the end,

40
00:01:53,958 --> 00:01:57,540
not just of our people, but all peoples.

41
00:02:00,708 --> 00:02:04,915
We are on the cusp of
crafting a new kind of power.

42
00:02:04,916 --> 00:02:07,165
Not of the flesh, but over flesh.

43
00:02:07,166 --> 00:02:09,415
All of a sudden, the two
of you seem quite familiar.

44
00:02:09,416 --> 00:02:11,915
I'm just offering
whatever humble aid I can.

45
00:02:13,166 --> 00:02:15,082
There is no King of the Southlands.

46
00:02:15,083 --> 00:02:16,249
The line was broken.

47
00:02:16,250 --> 00:02:17,707
Tell me your name.

48
00:02:17,708 --> 00:02:19,666
I have had many names.

49
00:02:20,666 --> 00:02:24,083
Sauron lives because of you!

50
00:02:34,250 --> 00:02:36,540
Galadriel, where is Halbrand?

51
00:02:36,541 --> 00:02:39,125
He is gone. And I doubt he will return.

52
00:02:40,125 --> 00:02:42,707
And should he ever, none of
us are to treat with him again.

53
00:02:42,708 --> 00:02:44,708
What happened by that stream?

54
00:03:52,583 --> 00:03:54,958
Always, after a defeat...

55
00:03:56,958 --> 00:04:00,625
the shadow takes another
shape and grows again.

56
00:04:03,583 --> 00:04:05,125
Morgoth is gone.

57
00:04:05,791 --> 00:04:08,833
Leaving us alone and disgraced.

58
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:13,250
But today, a new age begins.

59
00:04:14,125 --> 00:04:15,166
Under me.

60
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:17,875
Your new master.

61
00:04:19,000 --> 00:04:20,457
Sauron.

62
00:04:28,708 --> 00:04:32,750
And with a new age,
I bring a new vision.

63
00:04:34,750 --> 00:04:37,582
A path to unconditional conquest.

64
00:04:37,583 --> 00:04:40,333
For I seek a new kind of power.

65
00:04:41,791 --> 00:04:44,958
Not of the flesh, but over flesh.

66
00:04:47,041 --> 00:04:49,125
A power of the unseen world.

67
00:04:49,958 --> 00:04:51,891
One we shall use to enslave

68
00:04:51,892 --> 00:04:54,833
the peoples of Middle-earth
to our very will.

69
00:04:56,458 --> 00:04:58,082
Many Orcs will die.

70
00:05:00,833 --> 00:05:06,208
But out of the chaos, we will
forge a new and perfect order.

71
00:05:06,833 --> 00:05:11,790
No longer will we be hunted as
the demons who broke Middle-earth,

72
00:05:11,791 --> 00:05:17,040
but rather worshipped as the
saviors who finally healed it.

73
00:05:17,041 --> 00:05:22,415
By bringing its peoples
together, to rule them all as one!

74
00:05:22,416 --> 00:05:24,250
Sauron lies!

75
00:05:30,166 --> 00:05:31,666
Doubt me at your peril.

76
00:05:34,375 --> 00:05:37,833
You have nowhere else to turn.
The Valar will never forgive you.

77
00:05:38,333 --> 00:05:40,499
Elves will never accept you.

78
00:05:40,500 --> 00:05:41,958
Men...

79
00:05:43,333 --> 00:05:47,082
Men will never look upon you with
anything but horror and disgust.

80
00:05:47,083 --> 00:05:49,624
A corrupted and ignoble race,

81
00:05:49,625 --> 00:05:52,750
worthy only to be
hunted and slaughtered.

82
00:06:28,708 --> 00:06:34,583
I am your only future,
and my path your only path!

83
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:40,500
Who among you dare say otherwise?

84
00:07:04,416 --> 00:07:05,875
All Hail, Lord Sauron!

85
00:07:07,500 --> 00:07:09,416
The New Dark Lord.

86
00:07:12,166 --> 00:07:14,375
All hail!

87
00:10:49,166 --> 00:10:51,000
Hail Adar!

88
00:10:51,958 --> 00:10:53,333
Hail Adar!

89
00:10:54,375 --> 00:10:58,832
My children... you are free.

90
00:10:58,833 --> 00:11:02,082
Hail Adar! Hail Adar!

91
00:11:02,083 --> 00:11:10,083
Hail Adar! Hail Adar! Hail Adar!

92
00:16:23,875 --> 00:16:25,875
That way lies death, friend.

93
00:16:28,375 --> 00:16:29,791
Then that is my path.

94
00:16:30,541 --> 00:16:33,165
An army of Orcs moves against Men.

95
00:16:33,166 --> 00:16:34,749
We were the fortunate ones.

96
00:16:34,750 --> 00:16:37,041
Perhaps the fortunate
ones were the first to die.

97
00:16:40,458 --> 00:16:42,082
I know you've suffered.

98
00:16:42,083 --> 00:16:43,750
I can see it in your eyes.

99
00:16:44,583 --> 00:16:46,665
There's another life waiting for you.

100
00:16:46,666 --> 00:16:48,583
You just have to turn toward it.

101
00:16:51,166 --> 00:16:52,541
That heraldry.

102
00:16:54,166 --> 00:16:55,624
What is it?

103
00:16:55,625 --> 00:16:58,375
A symbol of kings, long-dead.

104
00:16:59,583 --> 00:17:00,833
- Your family?
- No.

105
00:17:02,375 --> 00:17:03,708
My family served them.

106
00:17:04,625 --> 00:17:06,000
Then why wear it?

107
00:17:06,125 --> 00:17:09,000
As a reminder that our
fates are never certain,

108
00:17:09,125 --> 00:17:12,250
that fortunes can turn,
for even the most powerful.

109
00:17:15,500 --> 00:17:16,500
A grim reminder.

110
00:17:17,333 --> 00:17:18,832
Or a hopeful one.

111
00:17:18,833 --> 00:17:21,666
A sure path may crumble,

112
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:24,583
but there's always another.

113
00:17:25,375 --> 00:17:28,458
Often, it can lead us someplace better.

114
00:17:30,708 --> 00:17:32,208
Someplace good.

115
00:17:35,458 --> 00:17:40,208
They say there's places across
the sea, a man can escape himself.

116
00:17:40,958 --> 00:17:42,250
Find another path.

117
00:17:42,958 --> 00:17:44,582
Perhaps another life.

118
00:17:44,583 --> 00:17:46,208
Come with us, if you like.

119
00:17:47,541 --> 00:17:49,875
Or, walk on.

120
00:17:51,375 --> 00:17:52,875
And keep chasing death.

121
00:17:58,833 --> 00:18:00,333
Choice is yours, friend.

122
00:18:53,375 --> 00:18:55,540
- Are you all right?
- No.

123
00:18:55,541 --> 00:18:57,083
Nightmares again?

124
00:18:58,541 --> 00:19:00,083
What haunts you so?

125
00:19:04,041 --> 00:19:05,250
I've done evil.

126
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:11,500
All of us have done things
that we care not to admit.

127
00:19:15,291 --> 00:19:16,708
Not like I have.

128
00:19:18,791 --> 00:19:20,415
Find forgiveness.

129
00:19:20,416 --> 00:19:24,291
You are alive because
you have chosen good.

130
00:19:24,916 --> 00:19:26,540
But what of tomorrow?

131
00:19:26,541 --> 00:19:28,791
You have to choose it again.

132
00:19:30,041 --> 00:19:33,041
And the next day. And the next.

133
00:19:33,875 --> 00:19:36,708
Until it becomes a part of your nature.

134
00:19:49,083 --> 00:19:50,749
- Grab hold of something.
- Ah!

135
00:19:50,750 --> 00:19:53,457
Help! Help me!

136
00:20:03,958 --> 00:20:05,083
Help me!

137
00:21:28,833 --> 00:21:29,833
Over here!

138
00:21:47,791 --> 00:21:50,583
The tides of fate are flowing.

139
00:21:51,500 --> 00:21:54,791
Yours may be heading in, or out.

140
00:22:50,458 --> 00:22:53,208
Elrond, stop, give them to me!

141
00:23:21,875 --> 00:23:24,125
We intend no insult,
Commander Galadriel,

142
00:23:24,750 --> 00:23:27,500
but by order of Herald Elrond,
you are to come with us.

143
00:23:53,833 --> 00:23:54,875
Is it true?

144
00:23:59,833 --> 00:24:01,000
High King.

145
00:24:05,250 --> 00:24:07,708
Herald Elrond carries three Rings.

146
00:24:08,875 --> 00:24:12,707
A means of halting the
fading and saving our people.

147
00:24:12,708 --> 00:24:16,416
We will discuss the Rings once
you have answered the question.

148
00:24:17,291 --> 00:24:21,124
Elrond just informed me your
companion, this Halbrand,

149
00:24:21,125 --> 00:24:22,957
was not who he claimed.

150
00:24:22,958 --> 00:24:26,791
Yet you chose to withhold
this from him and Celebrimbor.

151
00:24:27,291 --> 00:24:29,125
Is it true?

152
00:24:34,750 --> 00:24:35,750
Yes.

153
00:24:37,666 --> 00:24:39,208
Who is he?

154
00:24:40,083 --> 00:24:41,458
He is not what I thought.

155
00:24:42,333 --> 00:24:44,499
Which is the reason I did what I did.

156
00:24:44,500 --> 00:24:47,666
Why do you dance so to
avoid revealing the truth?

157
00:24:49,416 --> 00:24:50,750
High King

158
00:24:53,125 --> 00:24:56,416
You must believe I would never
knowingly endanger our kind.

159
00:24:57,083 --> 00:24:58,332
I will believe you

160
00:24:58,333 --> 00:25:01,958
when I no longer see
the lie behind your eyes.

161
00:25:03,041 --> 00:25:05,875
Now, who is this Man?

162
00:25:09,458 --> 00:25:10,958
He is no Man.

163
00:25:13,166 --> 00:25:17,166
He has been... masquerading as one.

164
00:25:19,458 --> 00:25:24,458
Appearing in fair form,
to hide his true self.

165
00:25:29,750 --> 00:25:31,041
He is Sauron.

166
00:25:44,208 --> 00:25:45,291
How could you?

167
00:25:48,000 --> 00:25:49,332
Of all our kind.

168
00:25:49,333 --> 00:25:52,124
He deceived me. I was deceived!

169
00:25:52,125 --> 00:25:56,415
No, Galadriel, you were blind.
Blinded by your own pride.

170
00:25:56,416 --> 00:25:59,000
- And what frailty blinded you, Elrond?
- Silence!

171
00:25:59,001 --> 00:26:00,499
What other path did your failure

172
00:26:00,500 --> 00:26:01,749
in Khazad-dûm leave us with?

173
00:26:01,750 --> 00:26:04,125
- You were my friend.
- Silence!

174
00:26:07,375 --> 00:26:10,457
The Rings. Show them to me.

175
00:26:10,458 --> 00:26:12,499
Dare not, High King.
He's no doubt corrupted...

176
00:26:12,500 --> 00:26:14,594
- He never touched them, High King.
- He worked with Celebrimbor

177
00:26:14,595 --> 00:26:17,332
for weeks. We know not
the depth of his influence.

178
00:26:17,333 --> 00:26:20,207
Soon, the last Gold-leaf will fall,

179
00:26:20,208 --> 00:26:24,582
and it will be my task to inform
all Lindon our time here is ended,

180
00:26:24,583 --> 00:26:28,290
and the Elves must abandon
these shores forever.

181
00:26:28,291 --> 00:26:32,000
Now, you inform me our most
cunning enemy is rising again.

182
00:26:32,708 --> 00:26:35,540
If we leave now, the
peoples of Middle-earth

183
00:26:35,541 --> 00:26:39,333
will be left to suffer under
the tyranny of a new Dark Lord.

184
00:26:40,000 --> 00:26:43,374
Those Rings are more than our last hope,

185
00:26:43,375 --> 00:26:45,957
they may be the last
hope for all Middle-earth.

186
00:26:45,958 --> 00:26:49,083
It is a risk we must chance to take.

187
00:26:49,708 --> 00:26:51,416
Give them to me.

188
00:26:54,083 --> 00:26:55,083
High King...

189
00:26:55,958 --> 00:26:58,707
Sauron has not yet amassed
that degree of power.

190
00:26:58,708 --> 00:27:01,249
These Rings may be how he attains it.

191
00:27:01,250 --> 00:27:03,207
They must be destroyed.

192
00:27:03,208 --> 00:27:07,374
That decision is far
above your privilege,

193
00:27:07,375 --> 00:27:11,041
one you endanger with each
moment you refuse to obey.

194
00:27:12,333 --> 00:27:14,333
The Rings, Elrond.

195
00:27:16,833 --> 00:27:19,540
It is a command from your King.

196
00:27:19,541 --> 00:27:21,374
I will not utter it again.

197
00:27:21,375 --> 00:27:23,165
Obey him.

198
00:27:23,166 --> 00:27:24,415
You would say that to me?

199
00:27:24,416 --> 00:27:26,833
It is the only way. Obey him!

200
00:27:43,375 --> 00:27:44,708
I cannot.

201
00:27:50,291 --> 00:27:51,750
You know I cannot.

202
00:27:52,958 --> 00:27:53,958
Seize him!

203
00:27:56,291 --> 00:27:57,582
Elrond, no!

204
00:28:05,458 --> 00:28:08,165
Find him. Find the rings.

205
00:28:08,166 --> 00:28:09,458
Go!

206
00:28:31,375 --> 00:28:32,958
Keep up! Move!

207
00:28:43,333 --> 00:28:45,291
Move those legs, king.

208
00:28:55,375 --> 00:28:56,874
Well, take that.

209
00:28:56,875 --> 00:28:59,249
Welcome to Mordor.

210
00:28:59,250 --> 00:29:02,124
Work its land well,
and you'll be fed well.

211
00:29:02,125 --> 00:29:05,416
Work it badly, and you'll feed the soil.

212
00:29:07,625 --> 00:29:13,291
You, lad, do you swear allegiance
to Adar, Lord-father of the Uruks?

213
00:29:20,083 --> 00:29:22,832
It is the Southlands no more!

214
00:29:22,833 --> 00:29:26,915
In Mordor, ya bow or ya bleed.

215
00:29:26,916 --> 00:29:31,000
Right, you there. Do you
swear allegiance to Adar?

216
00:29:47,166 --> 00:29:48,583
I'll take this one!

217
00:29:53,833 --> 00:29:57,790
The King of the Southlands
turned himself in, Lord-father.

218
00:29:57,791 --> 00:30:00,208
Says he wants to negotiate.

219
00:30:06,583 --> 00:30:08,291
Let my people go.

220
00:30:12,625 --> 00:30:13,916
Or yours will die.

221
00:30:17,416 --> 00:30:19,916
My people defeated
the Men of these lands.

222
00:30:21,291 --> 00:30:23,915
We defeated the Elves
who came to their aid.

223
00:30:23,916 --> 00:30:28,458
We even defeated their allies,
the Men from beyond the sea.

224
00:30:35,166 --> 00:30:37,375
There is no one left for us to fear.

225
00:30:39,125 --> 00:30:40,208
There is one.

226
00:30:41,666 --> 00:30:46,750
Since Galadriel's defeat,
she sought out a new ally.

227
00:30:47,333 --> 00:30:52,166
An ancient sorcerer, to instruct
the Elves in forging a new weapon.

228
00:30:54,875 --> 00:30:56,666
One you first told her about.

229
00:30:57,916 --> 00:30:59,750
A power over flesh.

230
00:31:01,791 --> 00:31:03,375
Do you remember those words?

231
00:31:04,041 --> 00:31:07,082
A power that will allow
him to use your children

232
00:31:07,083 --> 00:31:09,416
as slaves in his army once more.

233
00:31:10,500 --> 00:31:13,541
Set my people free, and I will
tell you where he can be found.

234
00:31:14,750 --> 00:31:19,208
So you can destroy him,
and rid us both of his evil.

235
00:31:20,958 --> 00:31:24,083
No, Your Majesty.

236
00:31:25,625 --> 00:31:29,583
You will tell me everything you
think you know of this sorcerer now.

237
00:31:31,375 --> 00:31:33,625
Or I will spill the
words from your throat.

238
00:31:35,000 --> 00:31:39,208
If I die, all that I know dies with me.

239
00:31:41,958 --> 00:31:43,375
You can't kill me.

240
00:31:45,541 --> 00:31:48,541
In time, you will beg me to.

241
00:31:50,750 --> 00:31:51,750
Ah!

242
00:31:56,166 --> 00:31:57,625
Your Majesty.

243
00:31:58,416 --> 00:31:59,540
Ha!

244
00:31:59,541 --> 00:32:01,832
What he said, Lord-father...

245
00:32:01,833 --> 00:32:06,499
Sauron... could never return, could he?

246
00:32:06,500 --> 00:32:07,583
No.

247
00:32:08,416 --> 00:32:10,082
Sauron is dead.

248
00:32:10,083 --> 00:32:11,583
On your knees, you maggots!

249
00:33:30,375 --> 00:33:31,916
You got that look in your eye.

250
00:33:37,583 --> 00:33:40,625
You had that dream again
last night, didn't you?

251
00:33:41,833 --> 00:33:45,541
If you tell me what it is you
keep seein', maybe I could...

252
00:33:46,666 --> 00:33:48,374
help you puzzle it out.

253
00:33:48,375 --> 00:33:51,583
Maybe it's a clue to what
we're going to find...

254
00:33:52,458 --> 00:33:54,333
when we reach those stars.

255
00:33:57,291 --> 00:33:59,250
It's the heat. That's all.

256
00:34:21,708 --> 00:34:24,125
No. It can't be.

257
00:34:25,833 --> 00:34:27,166
Stone trees.

258
00:34:29,250 --> 00:34:30,665
We're goin' in circles.

259
00:34:30,666 --> 00:34:35,499
There must be some evil upon
this land, confusing our path.

260
00:34:35,500 --> 00:34:37,499
Just admit it. We're lost.

261
00:34:37,500 --> 00:34:39,707
Panic is the fool's meal, Nori.

262
00:34:39,708 --> 00:34:42,124
We would be wiser to sup on patience.

263
00:34:42,125 --> 00:34:44,874
We haven't supped on anything
since we ran out of snails.

264
00:34:44,875 --> 00:34:46,583
There's nothin' to eat out here.

265
00:35:07,500 --> 00:35:09,333
Oh, no. Oh, no.

266
00:35:10,083 --> 00:35:11,083
Oh, come on.

267
00:35:11,541 --> 00:35:14,749
It might bear some fruit.
Least you could do is try.

268
00:35:14,750 --> 00:35:17,458
Have you forgotten what happened
when last I tried such a thing?

269
00:35:23,708 --> 00:35:24,708
Further.

270
00:35:33,791 --> 00:35:35,166
Further, Nori.

271
00:35:43,250 --> 00:35:44,333
All right?

272
00:36:24,916 --> 00:36:27,250
Ah!

273
00:36:37,208 --> 00:36:40,375
You did it. We'll eat for days.

274
00:36:58,541 --> 00:36:59,541
Don't be so glum.

275
00:36:59,542 --> 00:37:02,458
I asked you to conjure us
up some food, and you did.

276
00:37:03,125 --> 00:37:04,415
Nobody got hurt.

277
00:37:04,416 --> 00:37:05,708
I lost control.

278
00:37:06,583 --> 00:37:09,041
So you need to learn
how not to lose control.

279
00:37:11,625 --> 00:37:16,416
In the dream, there's
a kind of... branch.

280
00:37:17,750 --> 00:37:19,041
Under the stars.

281
00:37:19,750 --> 00:37:21,583
When I reach out to grasp it...

282
00:37:27,708 --> 00:37:30,708
What is it? What happens next?

283
00:37:33,625 --> 00:37:36,458
Some things are best not shared aloud.

284
00:37:38,208 --> 00:37:42,207
Except, well, you did
sort of share it aloud.

285
00:37:42,208 --> 00:37:44,999
So it's not rightly fair to be
all cryptic about it now, is it?

286
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:49,458
But perhaps, wizards
are not always fair.

287
00:37:54,041 --> 00:37:55,625
Hmm.

288
00:37:58,458 --> 00:37:59,583
Mmm.

289
00:38:01,084 --> 00:38:03,790
- I can feel the legs in the throat.
- That's the best part.

290
00:38:03,791 --> 00:38:04,916
They're dancin'.

291
00:38:05,708 --> 00:38:08,874
Poppy and I, we used
sing little buggy songs

292
00:38:08,875 --> 00:38:11,166
so they'd have music
to dance to when they...

293
00:38:16,291 --> 00:38:17,500
Well.

294
00:38:18,958 --> 00:38:21,666
It is quite all right for
a Harfoot to miss home.

295
00:38:23,083 --> 00:38:24,958
I knew it'd be hard. It's just, um...

296
00:38:28,416 --> 00:38:29,625
Well.

297
00:38:31,750 --> 00:38:33,250
This hard's different.

298
00:38:34,500 --> 00:38:36,160
Strange how that which is left behind

299
00:38:36,161 --> 00:38:39,541
can be the heaviest burden to carry.

300
00:38:43,166 --> 00:38:44,750
I miss my home, as well.

301
00:38:46,666 --> 00:38:48,291
You don't even remember yours.

302
00:38:48,791 --> 00:38:49,791
No.

303
00:38:53,250 --> 00:38:56,250
Sometimes, I perceive a
glimmer of it nonetheless.

304
00:38:56,875 --> 00:39:01,041
A longing for a feeling I
can't remember or even name.

305
00:39:04,500 --> 00:39:05,750
But I know it's real.

306
00:39:08,375 --> 00:39:10,083
Just beyond the sunset.

307
00:39:30,250 --> 00:39:31,874
It appears we're being followed.

308
00:40:21,000 --> 00:40:22,791
Come on, Your Majesty.

309
00:40:24,041 --> 00:40:27,625
Not even kings can go without food.

310
00:40:29,333 --> 00:40:30,750
Why don't you open up?

311
00:40:32,666 --> 00:40:37,583
You tell old Waldreg everything
you know about Sauron.

312
00:40:44,750 --> 00:40:48,291
Pain must be something you enjoy.

313
00:40:56,750 --> 00:41:00,208
After Lord-father releases
me, I'm going to kill you.

314
00:41:00,708 --> 00:41:03,541
Adar doesn't even remember you're here.

315
00:43:25,916 --> 00:43:26,916
Perfection.

316
00:43:27,416 --> 00:43:30,665
Perfection exists only in Valinor.

317
00:43:30,666 --> 00:43:32,250
Thank you, Master Círdan.

318
00:44:17,125 --> 00:44:18,875
You needn't hide any longer.

319
00:44:26,666 --> 00:44:28,083
Master Círdan.

320
00:44:36,458 --> 00:44:39,041
Please forgive the
unexpected nature of my visit,

321
00:44:40,416 --> 00:44:42,165
but I have nowhere else to turn.

322
00:44:42,166 --> 00:44:45,125
You are the oldest
and wisest of our kind.

323
00:44:45,875 --> 00:44:48,583
And the Elves are facing
our greatest test in an age.

324
00:44:50,625 --> 00:44:53,249
I perceive you carry
something in your charge.

325
00:44:53,250 --> 00:44:56,166
Something louder than the sea.

326
00:44:57,041 --> 00:44:58,249
What have you brought here?

327
00:45:04,500 --> 00:45:07,582
It is to be given directly
to Lord Celebrimbor.

328
00:45:07,583 --> 00:45:09,374
He must be informed

329
00:45:09,375 --> 00:45:11,999
that Halbrand is Sauron.

330
00:45:12,000 --> 00:45:13,750
Move with haste,

331
00:45:14,333 --> 00:45:16,791
and trust no stranger upon your path.

332
00:45:17,416 --> 00:45:18,666
Yes, my lord.

333
00:45:31,875 --> 00:45:35,165
I have yet to thank you. For
trusting me, regarding the Rings.

334
00:45:35,166 --> 00:45:36,666
Trusting you?

335
00:45:38,291 --> 00:45:39,791
Let us be clear, Commander.

336
00:45:40,625 --> 00:45:43,875
You and I are momentarily
aligned for one reason,

337
00:45:44,375 --> 00:45:47,250
because your actions have
left us no alternative.

338
00:45:47,958 --> 00:45:51,375
Because of you, our enemy lives.

339
00:45:52,291 --> 00:45:55,290
Because of you, we've no choice
but to test the virtue of the Rings.

340
00:45:55,291 --> 00:45:56,874
I should have you thrown in fetters

341
00:45:56,875 --> 00:45:58,707
and cast to the Ettenmoors
for what you've done.

342
00:45:58,708 --> 00:46:00,416
Then why have you not?

343
00:46:03,708 --> 00:46:05,333
I am considering it.

344
00:46:14,916 --> 00:46:16,666
I swear to you, High King,

345
00:46:18,208 --> 00:46:22,541
I will not stop until he is
destroyed and I have put this right.

346
00:46:25,541 --> 00:46:28,125
You would not be here now
if I thought otherwise.

347
00:46:33,250 --> 00:46:35,625
High King, we have not found the Rings.

348
00:46:36,625 --> 00:46:39,208
We've scoured everywhere
water meets rock, and yet,

349
00:46:40,000 --> 00:46:41,375
there's no trace of him.

350
00:46:42,291 --> 00:46:44,125
- Perhaps the fall...
- No.

351
00:46:45,166 --> 00:46:46,416
Elrond lives.

352
00:46:48,041 --> 00:46:49,666
Expand the search.

353
00:46:50,166 --> 00:46:53,833
Set a watch at every
crossing. He must not escape.

354
00:46:58,583 --> 00:47:00,458
Escape is not his plan.

355
00:47:02,250 --> 00:47:03,458
Meaning?

356
00:47:04,583 --> 00:47:06,875
He spoke of destroying the Rings.

357
00:47:07,500 --> 00:47:09,833
Elrond would seek out
someone he can trust.

358
00:47:10,541 --> 00:47:13,208
Someone older, wiser...

359
00:47:14,500 --> 00:47:16,500
Whose voice would command respect.

360
00:47:17,625 --> 00:47:19,250
Even from you.

361
00:47:19,833 --> 00:47:23,041
Someone who could
turn the tides his way.

362
00:47:28,958 --> 00:47:30,458
You may examine them.

363
00:47:32,291 --> 00:47:34,208
I've seen Celebrimbor's work before.

364
00:47:35,625 --> 00:47:37,625
- He's remarkable.
- He is.

365
00:47:38,458 --> 00:47:40,260
I remember, he used
to speak of, one day,

366
00:47:40,261 --> 00:47:42,457
crafting objects of such power,

367
00:47:42,458 --> 00:47:45,166
they could change the heart
of any who beheld them.

368
00:47:47,000 --> 00:47:49,665
If, as you say,

369
00:47:49,666 --> 00:47:53,875
these Rings have so quickly
turned Elf against Elf...

370
00:47:56,583 --> 00:47:58,291
it would appear he has succeeded.

371
00:47:59,750 --> 00:48:03,041
Perhaps it was not Celebrimbor's
hand that produced that effect.

372
00:48:04,375 --> 00:48:06,125
If what you've told me is true,

373
00:48:07,083 --> 00:48:11,166
these three Rings were
made without Sauron's touch.

374
00:48:11,833 --> 00:48:13,250
The Enemy is cunning.

375
00:48:14,041 --> 00:48:16,457
The Rings may well
be a ploy on his part.

376
00:48:16,458 --> 00:48:19,916
A device in some larger plan, the
end of which we cannot yet see.

377
00:48:25,666 --> 00:48:27,291
What would you ask of me?

378
00:48:28,666 --> 00:48:30,541
The Rings must be destroyed.

379
00:48:31,666 --> 00:48:34,541
Do so, and the Age
of the Elves will end.

380
00:48:37,333 --> 00:48:41,625
We would be abandoning all
Middle-earth to its fate.

381
00:48:42,666 --> 00:48:43,790
Could you accept that?

382
00:48:43,791 --> 00:48:48,083
If to do otherwise means falling
prey to the designs of the Enemy...

383
00:48:49,375 --> 00:48:50,375
Yes.

384
00:48:51,583 --> 00:48:53,333
You do your father proud.

385
00:49:05,125 --> 00:49:06,708
Long ago, there was a battle.

386
00:49:08,416 --> 00:49:11,582
One whose weapons were the
very bones of the continents.

387
00:49:11,583 --> 00:49:14,499
Still now, at the spot
where our bay meets the sea,

388
00:49:14,500 --> 00:49:17,374
there remains on the
seabed a scar so deep,

389
00:49:17,375 --> 00:49:20,249
its end none but Manwë himself knows.

390
00:49:20,250 --> 00:49:25,165
If one were to cast these
Rings into its depths, they...

391
00:49:38,375 --> 00:49:39,916
Let me speak with him first.

392
00:49:41,166 --> 00:49:42,583
Please, High King.

393
00:49:44,000 --> 00:49:47,541
Give me one last chance
to reason with my friend?

394
00:49:48,958 --> 00:49:50,541
Reason quickly.

395
00:49:58,541 --> 00:49:59,625
Elrond?

396
00:50:01,708 --> 00:50:03,500
I have come to coax you willingly.

397
00:50:04,000 --> 00:50:07,000
If I fail, the High King
will see you removed by force.

398
00:50:12,125 --> 00:50:14,083
I have failed enough
of late, old friend.

399
00:50:15,583 --> 00:50:17,250
Help me succeed this time?

400
00:50:20,583 --> 00:50:25,000
I should have trusted you,
as I asked you to trust me.

401
00:50:26,666 --> 00:50:30,500
But unless we both trust in
the Rings now, all will be lost.

402
00:50:33,000 --> 00:50:34,625
With three, there is balance.

403
00:50:35,958 --> 00:50:36,958
Don't you remember?

404
00:50:37,708 --> 00:50:39,500
We chose this path together.

405
00:50:41,500 --> 00:50:44,207
- No, you chose it for me.
- Elrond...

406
00:50:44,208 --> 00:50:46,124
What so frightens you,
you cannot consider

407
00:50:46,125 --> 00:50:47,708
the possibility of their corruption?

408
00:50:50,083 --> 00:50:51,583
Because in my heart,

409
00:50:52,833 --> 00:50:55,666
I know The Three Rings
are free of his influence.

410
00:50:56,458 --> 00:50:57,541
But are you?

411
00:51:00,083 --> 00:51:04,375
The light of Valinor shone
upon your very face, Galadriel,

412
00:51:05,041 --> 00:51:06,666
and you turned your back on it.

413
00:51:08,083 --> 00:51:12,374
Was it truly to fight the darkness
or was the darkness calling to you?

414
00:51:12,375 --> 00:51:15,582
Can you not see? All
this may be by his design.

415
00:51:15,583 --> 00:51:17,708
I did what I felt was right.

416
00:51:19,666 --> 00:51:23,666
And time alone will reveal
whether that was folly or wisdom.

417
00:51:26,625 --> 00:51:29,083
What time do you think you have?

418
00:51:31,791 --> 00:51:33,208
Where is Círdan?

419
00:51:33,916 --> 00:51:35,916
You did what you must, Galadriel.

420
00:51:38,708 --> 00:51:40,082
So have I.

421
00:51:40,083 --> 00:51:41,416
Elrond.

422
00:51:42,708 --> 00:51:44,540
Where are the Rings?

423
00:53:05,291 --> 00:53:06,291
Huh?

424
00:53:14,416 --> 00:53:15,957
Poppy!

425
00:53:18,458 --> 00:53:20,707
Mmm, honey biscuits.

426
00:53:20,708 --> 00:53:22,708
Never been happier in
my life than right now.

427
00:53:26,916 --> 00:53:28,666
How's everyone at home?

428
00:53:30,291 --> 00:53:31,415
About the same.

429
00:53:31,416 --> 00:53:33,374
Your ma took to giving me your chores,

430
00:53:33,375 --> 00:53:35,208
but your da said I
didn't have to do 'em.

431
00:53:38,916 --> 00:53:40,333
You came after us.

432
00:53:41,000 --> 00:53:44,124
Wasn't so hard. You haven't
exactly gotten very far.

433
00:53:44,125 --> 00:53:45,582
Yes, well, we appear to be lost.

434
00:53:45,583 --> 00:53:46,999
So now you admit it.

435
00:53:47,000 --> 00:53:49,166
Well, you won't be for long. Look.

436
00:53:51,208 --> 00:53:52,915
I was sifting through Sadoc's old book.

437
00:53:52,916 --> 00:53:55,499
Harfoots must've journeyed
this way a long time ago.

438
00:53:55,500 --> 00:53:57,207
See, there's a warnin',

439
00:53:57,208 --> 00:53:59,045
"Not to forget the words to the song,

440
00:53:59,046 --> 00:54:00,749
or you'll just go round in circles."

441
00:54:00,750 --> 00:54:02,790
Song? What song?

442
00:54:02,791 --> 00:54:03,915
Give you one guess.

443
00:54:03,916 --> 00:54:08,125
Sing to me, sing to me, land far away

444
00:54:09,458 --> 00:54:11,874
- The walkin' song?
- I think it's some kinda directions.

445
00:54:11,875 --> 00:54:13,582
Our folk have been wanderin' for years.

446
00:54:13,583 --> 00:54:15,790
Guess this path must have
been important to them.

447
00:54:15,791 --> 00:54:17,625
I say, we climb.

448
00:54:18,500 --> 00:54:23,666
"Trees of stone... Light in
the tower, no longer my home."

449
00:54:30,125 --> 00:54:31,125
There.

450
00:54:36,375 --> 00:54:38,208
"Past eyes of pale fire."

451
00:54:40,916 --> 00:54:42,666
"Black sand for my bed."

452
00:54:45,916 --> 00:54:49,291
"I trade all I've known
for the unknown ahead."

453
00:55:07,125 --> 00:55:09,541
Welcome to the lands of Rhûn.

454
00:55:10,708 --> 00:55:13,125
Come on. What are you waitin' for?

455
00:55:14,125 --> 00:55:15,625
This is only the beginnin'.

456
00:55:23,041 --> 00:55:24,708
Why you looking at it like that?

457
00:55:26,833 --> 00:55:28,000
Like what?

458
00:55:28,583 --> 00:55:30,458
Like you've been here before.

459
00:55:33,333 --> 00:55:34,750
Only in dreams.

460
00:57:14,916 --> 00:57:16,416
I was in your place once.

461
00:57:20,958 --> 00:57:22,958
In the eldest of the Elder Days.

462
00:57:27,666 --> 00:57:32,124
Thirteen of us were chosen to
be blessed of Morgoth's hand,

463
00:57:32,125 --> 00:57:34,041
with the promise of power.

464
00:57:36,000 --> 00:57:37,416
A new birth.

465
00:57:41,708 --> 00:57:45,165
I was led up to a
dark and nameless peak.

466
00:57:45,166 --> 00:57:47,541
Chained and left.

467
00:57:49,208 --> 00:57:53,916
And after what seemed
endless thirst and hunger...

468
00:57:56,958 --> 00:57:58,166
I saw it.

469
00:58:01,333 --> 00:58:02,875
His servant's face.

470
00:58:05,375 --> 00:58:07,083
Sauron's face.

471
00:58:09,291 --> 00:58:11,708
And it was beautiful.

472
00:58:14,166 --> 00:58:17,375
He offered me wine, red as a blood moon.

473
00:58:20,666 --> 00:58:24,208
He offered me wine, and on
that dark and nameless peak,

474
00:58:26,125 --> 00:58:27,166
I drank it.

475
00:58:27,583 --> 00:58:28,958
I drank it all.

476
00:58:33,791 --> 00:58:35,708
Your people have been set free.

477
00:58:38,791 --> 00:58:41,000
Now, tell me what you know of Sauron.

478
00:58:46,375 --> 00:58:48,875
Sauron has returned in a new form.

479
00:58:50,625 --> 00:58:54,082
I am not yet certain
what shape he has taken.

480
00:58:54,083 --> 00:58:55,833
Then of what use are you to me?

481
00:58:56,750 --> 00:58:58,832
I have something you don't.

482
00:58:58,833 --> 00:59:00,416
The trust of the Elves.

483
00:59:01,416 --> 00:59:02,875
Release me,

484
00:59:04,541 --> 00:59:06,458
and I'll go to them and seek him out,

485
00:59:07,041 --> 00:59:09,750
so you can marshal your
legions to destroy him.

486
00:59:26,625 --> 00:59:30,208
Do you vow allegiance to Adar,

487
00:59:30,875 --> 00:59:33,125
Lord-father of the Uruks?

488
00:59:40,750 --> 00:59:42,125
Yes.

489
00:59:44,791 --> 00:59:46,250
Then kneel.

490
01:00:02,625 --> 01:00:04,000
Now, swear it.

491
01:00:07,500 --> 01:00:10,333
- I vow...
- With your head at my feet.

492
01:00:26,000 --> 01:00:28,458
I vow to serve the Lord of Mordor.

493
01:00:31,875 --> 01:00:33,541
To the end of my days...

494
01:00:35,875 --> 01:00:36,916
and his.

495
01:00:52,625 --> 01:00:54,750
What're you doing? Keep away.

496
01:00:58,500 --> 01:01:00,666
See that he's followed. Every step.

497
01:01:02,833 --> 01:01:04,833
"I'm going to kill you."

498
01:01:06,375 --> 01:01:08,416
Is that right, Your Majesty?

499
01:01:09,625 --> 01:01:11,540
All hail the king.

500
01:01:11,541 --> 01:01:12,875
Oh!

501
01:01:35,541 --> 01:01:38,207
O Elven-kind!

502
01:01:38,208 --> 01:01:44,291
Too long have we dwelt
Upon this Hither Shore

503
01:01:46,458 --> 01:01:51,832
And now, a fading crown...

504
01:01:51,833 --> 01:01:57,457
Must trade, to sail to Valinor

505
01:01:57,458 --> 01:02:05,458
O Elven-kind!

506
01:02:07,750 --> 01:02:10,665
The Winter comes

507
01:02:10,666 --> 01:02:16,750
The bare and leafless day...

508
01:02:19,333 --> 01:02:27,333
O Elven-kind!

509
01:02:30,000 --> 01:02:32,957
The leaves are falling in the stream

510
01:02:32,958 --> 01:02:39,041
The river flows away

511
01:02:44,791 --> 01:02:48,625
The light of the Eldar has faded.

512
01:02:49,166 --> 01:02:52,416
As coals too long
removed from the hearth,

513
01:02:53,250 --> 01:02:58,707
we must return to our home or
diminish forever into endless night.

514
01:02:58,708 --> 01:03:01,166
And so it is come to pass,

515
01:03:01,750 --> 01:03:06,208
our days in Middle-earth... are ended.

516
01:03:31,833 --> 01:03:35,750
Perfection does not exist
only in Valinor, High King.

517
01:03:37,458 --> 01:03:38,750
It is here.

518
01:03:39,458 --> 01:03:42,625
Celebrimbor has brought
it to Middle-earth.

519
01:03:55,458 --> 01:03:56,750
No!

520
01:04:23,208 --> 01:04:24,708
Galadriel.

521
01:04:28,500 --> 01:04:29,750
No.

522
01:07:37,083 --> 01:07:40,333
The new forge is remarkable, my lord.

523
01:07:41,750 --> 01:07:43,582
It is, indeed.

524
01:07:43,583 --> 01:07:47,958
Let us pray the Rings worked,
so we have a chance to use it.

525
01:07:49,208 --> 01:07:52,541
Forgive me, my lord, but a
messenger has just arrived.

526
01:07:53,375 --> 01:07:55,040
Word from Lindon?

527
01:07:55,041 --> 01:07:58,707
To the contrary, my lord. This
messenger is from the Southlands.

528
01:07:58,708 --> 01:08:01,375
He says he wants to negotiate.

529
01:08:29,250 --> 01:08:31,957
Well, my lord? Do we grant him entry?

530
01:09:07,708 --> 01:09:09,833
I have seen mountains crumbling.

531
01:09:10,833 --> 01:09:12,291
Waters running dry.

532
01:09:13,083 --> 01:09:16,082
And clouds. Black.
Gathering over white towers.

533
01:09:21,750 --> 01:09:22,750
A storm is coming.

534
01:09:23,708 --> 01:09:24,832
Prepare yourselves.

535
01:09:24,833 --> 01:09:27,750
I am waiting for you.

536
01:09:34,666 --> 01:09:36,124
Something has awoken them.

537
01:09:36,125 --> 01:09:38,583
No. Someone.

538
01:09:39,625 --> 01:09:41,457
It is said he has taken a new form

539
01:09:41,458 --> 01:09:43,540
to deceive his enemies.

540
01:09:43,541 --> 01:09:46,041
- Who are you?
- Annatar.

541
01:09:46,500 --> 01:09:47,875
Lord of Gifts.

542
01:09:49,666 --> 01:09:53,625
Sauron is alone, without army or ally.

543
01:09:54,625 --> 01:09:57,625
He needs not armies... but Rings.

544
01:09:59,166 --> 01:10:03,541
Seven Rings. Seven Dwarves.
And bound within each, power.

545
01:10:06,375 --> 01:10:08,790
You saved the Elves. Make Rings for Men.

546
01:10:08,791 --> 01:10:11,332
We cannot give Rings to Men.

547
01:10:11,333 --> 01:10:14,375
The risk of corruption
is simply too great.

548
01:10:15,875 --> 01:10:18,958
True creation requires sacrifice.

549
01:10:22,166 --> 01:10:24,165
In choosing to wear those Rings,

550
01:10:24,166 --> 01:10:26,832
you have all chosen to
become his collaborators.

551
01:10:26,833 --> 01:10:28,165
Take off the Ring.

552
01:10:32,333 --> 01:10:34,500
I will defeat him. At any cost.

553
01:10:35,250 --> 01:10:37,250
No! This is what Sauron wants!

554
01:10:39,833 --> 01:10:42,415
I've felt bound. To try
and do something special.

555
01:10:42,416 --> 01:10:44,541
You must remain calm at the storm's eye.

556
01:10:46,583 --> 01:10:48,957
This magic. Can you teach it to me?

557
01:10:48,958 --> 01:10:50,666
If you prove yourself worthy of it.

558
01:10:57,458 --> 01:11:01,040
Sauron rises in the west.
A Dark Wizard in the east.

559
01:11:01,041 --> 01:11:04,083
Every soul in Middle-earth is in peril.

560
01:11:04,583 --> 01:11:06,666
Will you abandon them to their doom?

561
01:11:07,333 --> 01:11:08,790
Together we can put this right.

562
01:11:08,791 --> 01:11:11,041
- Nobody goes off-trail.
- Nobody walks alone.

563
01:11:15,833 --> 01:11:18,041
I need your axe, old
friend. I need it now.

564
01:11:20,875 --> 01:11:23,416
Celebrimbor, you and I have work to do.

565
01:11:32,667 --> 01:11:37,667
